@bank all
// Head writer 0607: the words on the time clock's new pop-up screen (player engineer 6's), in the device's art style:
// short, upper-case headings like an old ship terminal, plain sentences below. TEXTS: said by nobody.
// {time} a clock time ("08:02"), {hours} a count of hours ("7.5"), {day} a weekday.

== clock.screen.title
- WORKS TIME CLOCK

== clock.screen.sub
- CSV Wren · Works bay

== clock.screen.in
- Clock in

== clock.screen.out
- Clock out

== clock.screen.close
- Close

== clock.screen.ready
- Shift starts at {time}. Tap to clock in.

== clock.screen.onshift
- On shift since {time}.

== clock.screen.offshift
- Off shift.

== clock.screen.didin
- Clocked in at {time}. Have a good shift.

== clock.screen.didout
- Clocked out at {time}. Evening's yours.

== clock.screen.late
- Clocked in at {time}. A little late. It happens.

== clock.screen.early
- Before 17:00. Clock out early?

== clock.screen.hours
- YOUR HOURS

== clock.screen.today
- Today: {hours} h

== clock.screen.week
- This week: {hours} h

== clock.screen.day
- {weekday}: {hours} h

== clock.screen.offday
- Day off. No clocking today.

== clock.screen.leave
- On leave today. Enjoy it.

== clock.screen.sick
- Off sick. Get well.

== clock.screen.done
- Shift done. See you tomorrow.

== clock.screen.weekend
- Shift done. See you Monday.
